<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jaswant Singh of Marwar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1626–1678</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Jaswant Singh I of Jodhpur</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jaswant Singh was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rathore">Rathore</a> ruler of Marwar, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jodhpur">Jodhpur</a>, from 1638 to 1678 and a senior commander of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughal Empire</a>. He served <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shah-jahan">Shah Jahan</a> and later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aurangzeb">Aurangzeb</a>, campaigning in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan">Deccan</a> and on the north-west frontier, where he died. When Aurangzeb tried to take over Marwar after his death, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/durgadas-rathore">Durgadas Rathore</a> led a long resistance on behalf of his posthumous son Ajit Singh.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jaswant-singh-of-marwar.jpg" alt="Jaswant Singh of Marwar" width="220" height="308" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jaswant_Singh_of_Marwar.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
